id: pm-rzs24j
title: "Official MCP tasks extension for pm: asynchronous long operations, tasks/get polling, tasks/update input, durable handles, and lifecycle convergence"
description: "Expose long-running pm operations through io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks with SDK-owned durable handles, polling, mid-flight input, cancellation, expiration, and immutable lifecycle evidence."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:mcp","area:sdk",async,durable-handles,long-running,tasks-extension
created_at: "2026-08-25T05:09:28.783Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-25T05:09:28.783Z"
deadline: "2026-11-15T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 900
acceptance_criteria: "The tasks extension is explicitly negotiated and never appears as an unadvertised core capability; Eligible long operations can return durable handles without per-request opt-in and tasks/get reports bounded authoritative state; tasks/update accepts validated mid-flight input and composes deterministically with MRTR inputResponses; tasks/list and blocking tasks/result are not implemented on the canonical 2026-07-28 path; Cancellation, duplicate updates, expiration, unauthorized access, restart recovery, retention, and immutable terminal evidence have negative tests; The SDK provides a transport-neutral task provider and adapters for test, reindex, graph, import, and validation operations"
goal: Standard asynchronous execution for long pm operations
objective: "Map tests, reindexing, graph analysis, imports, validation, and other bounded long operations onto the official tasks extension"
value: "Hosts can start, inspect, steer, cancel, and recover long pm work without blocking a request or inventing a private job protocol"
why_now: "2026-07-28 moves tasks out of core and redesigns them around tasks/get, tasks/update, unsolicited handles, and extension negotiation"
parent: pm-rs9vry
risk: high
confidence: medium
