comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T05:09:28.783Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks tasks/get tasks/update tasks/result tasks/list durable handles polling and mid-flight input. Existing pm task and plan items are domain lifecycle work and do not implement the MCP extension."
body: "## Task lifecycle\n\n- A qualifying operation may return a durable task handle when the tasks extension is negotiated.\n- tasks/get polls authoritative status, bounded progress, result, error, expiration, and recovery.\n- tasks/update supplies mid-flight client input and composes with MRTR without two conflicting state machines.\n- Cancellation and timeout are idempotent and terminal task states are immutable events.\n- Handles are scoped to workspace, authority, protocol policy, and retention; they never expose filesystem paths or secrets.\n- Existing pm plan, test-run, telemetry, and history identifiers remain domain records and are not silently conflated with transport task handles."
